{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA644571","title":"Positive Effects of Zeolite Powder on Aerobic Granulation: Nitrogen and Phosphorus Removal and Insights into the Interaction Mechanism","description":"Aerobic granular sludge is considered to be one of the most promising biological wastewater treatment technologies of the 21st century. However, the long granulation time and poor treatment effect on N and P have severely limited its popularization and large-scale application. In this study, we systematically examined the strengthening effects of zeolite powder on granulation and N and P removal, and their interaction mechanism. The addition of zeolite powder shortened the sludge granulation time to 18 days and improved the average N and P removal rates by 4.48% and 2.22%, respectively. This is the result of the combined action of physical, chemical, and biological factors. The multi-pore and nutrient-rich environment of zeolite powder are beneficial to the maintenance of microbial activity and granule stability. Moreover, its adsorption to N and P enriches their respective removal strains, thereby improving their removal effect.","center":"College of Chemistry and Environmental Engineering","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2020/07/07 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN15464255","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2019-08-14",2019,"CN","Beijing",1816670,"Beijing","probable",39.91,116.41,"China: Shenzhen","sludge sample",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN15464256","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2019-08-14",2019,"CN","Beijing",1816670